      "created_at": "2016-12-18T12:16:04Z",
      "updated_at": "2016-12-18T12:16:04Z",
      "body": "The existing method should remain otherwise we break backwards compatibility. If you are willing so, please do a PR and document the flow as you described in the pseudo-code here since it is quite important to clarify what happens when the existing object already contains either username/password/permissions.\r\n\r\nNow I think we should only throw error if the generated fields exists and are different from the mongoauth managed ones. Say if the username is the same it could be ok not to throw error but ignore and continue, same for roles/permissions **BUT** not for passwords, that should always be managed by the auth provider.\r\n\r\nWDYT?",
